;; Counting words: string scanning feeding a mutable map with a default.
;;
;; `words` is a generator built from a scan, and `map({}, 0)` is a mutable map whose missing keys
;; read as 0. `every` drives the generator through the whole text, so each word's count starts from
;; 0 the first time it is seen, and the assignment adds the word. A map keeps its keys in the order
;; they were first added, so the counts come out in first-seen order.

val text = 'the cat sat. the cat ran! a dog sat, and the dog ran; the end.'

def words( s )
  s ?
    while tab( upto(letters) )
      val w = tab( many(letters) )
      yield w

val counts = map( {}, 0 )

every counts( words(text) ) += 1

for (w, n) <- !counts
  write( w, n )

;; the, 4 / cat, 2 / sat, 2 / ran, 2 / a, 1 / dog, 2 / and, 1 / end, 1
